# CAD Output — shared DXF drawing library for AutoCAD LT

---

## What This Is

Not a user-facing skill. This file documents `tools/cad-output/dxf_writer.py`,
the shared library **every drawing skill must use** to produce AutoCAD LT
drawings. AutoCAD LT has no COM interface, so skills never draw live —
they build a `.dxf` with this library and hand it to LT.

---

## Rules for skill scripts

1. Import the library — do not call ezdxf directly for layers, styles or saving:
   ```python
   import sys, pathlib
   sys.path.insert(0, str(pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "cad-output"))
   import dxf_writer as dw
   ```
2. Start every drawing with `dw.new_drawing(text_height=2.5, scale=<1:scale>)`.
3. Draw only on the standard layers (below).
4. Save with `dw.save(doc, project_number, name)` — it audits the file and
   writes to `Projects/[project-number]/`, never overwriting (adds `_01`, `_02`...).
5. Open with `dw.open_in_lt(path)` and report the returned `reason`:
   - `STARTED` — LT launched with the file.
   - `LT_ALREADY_RUNNING` — tell the user the path and to open it in LT
     (OPEN, or drag into the window). Never start a second LT instance.
   - `LT_NOT_FOUND` — report it.

---

## API summary

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `new_drawing(text_height, scale, layers=None)` | New drawing with layers, STRUCT text style and STRUCT dim style. Model text height = text_height × scale. `layers` = {name: (colour, linetype, lineweight)} replaces the default structural layers (use it for electrical sheets). |
| `line`, `polyline`, `rect`, `circle` | Basic geometry (layer default `CONCRETE`). |
| `bar_section(msp, centre, bar_dia)` | Solid-filled bar in section on `REO`. |
| `hatch_concrete(msp, points)` | AR-CONC hatch on `HATCH`. |
| `text`, `mtext` | Text on `TEXT` in STRUCT style; default height from the drawing scale. |
| `dim_linear(msp, p1, p2, offset, angle=None)` | Linear dimension on `DIM`. |
| `leader_text(msp, content, target, text_pos)` | Line + label on `REO-TEXT`. |
| `save(doc, project, name)` | Audit + save to `Projects/[project]/[name].dxf`. |
| `open_in_lt(path)` / `reveal(path)` | Open in LT / show in Explorer. |
| `find_lt()` / `lt_running()` | LT install & process detection. |

## Standard layers

| Layer | Colour | Linetype | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| CONCRETE | 7 | Continuous | Concrete outlines |
| HIDDEN | 8 | HIDDEN | Hidden edges |
| CENTRE | 1 | CENTER | Centrelines / grids |
| REO | 1 | Continuous | Reinforcement |
| REO-TEXT | 2 | Continuous | Bar marks / labels |
| DIM | 3 | Continuous | Dimensions |
| TEXT | 7 | Continuous | Notes, titles |
| HATCH | 8 | Continuous | Hatching |
| BORDER | 7 | Continuous | Frames / title blocks |

---

## Dependencies

- Python 3.10+ (installed: 3.15)
- `python -m pip install ezdxf` (installed: 1.4.4)

---

## LOCK

```bash
python tools/cad-output/tests/run_lock.py
```

Compares against `tools/cad-output/tests/expected_results.json`
(header/units, layers, geometry, dimension values, text, save naming).

